From 3f0bacb1b69e4fe2b58d06cc91d99c1ced9121cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: consnop <consnop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:09:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] voice: pick the spoken language on the dictation screen

Phone-side transcription with auto-detection often guesses the wrong
language for short phrases. The dictation screen now shows an SK / EN / DE
row under the status bar; Up and Down cycle it, wrapping around, at any
point while the screen is up. The choice is kept in the dictationLanguage
pref (default English) and sent to the phone:

- with the session setup, as attribute 0x40 holding the two-letter
  ISO 639-1 code;
- when it changes during a session, as voice endpoint message 0x40
  (flags, session id, attribute list with the same attribute).

Both ids are outside upstream's ranges. Phones that don't know them ignore
the attribute; the message is new and only consnop's Gravel handles it.

VoiceWindow keeps its applib_malloc size: the row's layer is allocated
separately and its padding absorbs the new pointer and byte. The pref is
written from the system work queue rather than the app's syscall.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: consnop <consnop@users.noreply.github.com>
